<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Training Details</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use the code implementation of VLM training from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Karamcheti et al. (2024)</a></cite>, as it allows for flexible changes to the image encoder and LM backbone components.
We adopt the hyperparameters in <a href="#A1.T1" title="In Appendix A Training Details ‣ Cross-Modal Taxonomic Generalization in (Vision-) Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> for all our experiments.
Model training is conducted on a GPU cluster using 4 RTX A6000/RTX 6000 Ada/L40S/RTX Pro 6000 GPUs, depending on availability.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T1" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A1.T1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A1.T1.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T1.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="A1.T1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hyperparameter</span></th>
<th id="A1.T1.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A1.T1.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Value</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A1.T1.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T1.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">Epochs</th>
<td id="A1.T1.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_t">5</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T1.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T1.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Batch Size</th>
<td id="A1.T1.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right">16</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T1.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T1.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Number of Layers</th>
<td id="A1.T1.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right">2</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T1.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T1.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Input Dimension</th>
<td id="A1.T1.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right">1024/1152</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T1.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T1.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Output Dimension</th>
<td id="A1.T1.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right">1024/2048</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T1.2.7" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T1.2.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Max Gradient Norm</th>
<td id="A1.T1.2.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right">1.0</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T1.2.8" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T1.2.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Weight Decay</th>
<td id="A1.T1.2.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right">0.1</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T1.2.9" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T1.2.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Learning Rate</th>
<td id="A1.T1.2.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right"><math id="A1.T1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\times 10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times 10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T1.2.10" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T1.2.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Activation Function</th>
<td id="A1.T1.2.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right">GeLU</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T1.2.11" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T1.2.11.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Optimizer</th>
<td id="A1.T1.2.11.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right">AdamW</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T1.2.12" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T1.2.12.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Scheduler</th>
<td id="A1.T1.2.12.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right">Warmup &amp; Cosine Decay</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T1.2.13" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T1.2.13.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb">Warmup Ratio</th>
<td id="A1.T1.2.13.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb">0.03</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>Training hyperparameters used in our experiments. We adopt a <math id="A1.T1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>-layer multi-layer perceptron architecture with GeLU activation for all vision-language projectors. The input dimension of our trained MLP projectors is 1024 for DINOv2 and 1152 for SigLIP.
The output dimension of our trained MLP projectors is 1024 for Qwen3-0.6B, and 2048 for all other LM backbones. The two MLP layers share the same output dimension across experiments.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Details of Experimental Data</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Data Use and Release Policy</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use images from the THINGS database for our experimental data <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hebart et al., 2019</a>)</cite>. These images were released with the Attribution CC BY license.<span id="footnote2" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">2</span>
              
              
              
              
              
              
              
            See <a href="https://osf.io/jum2f/files/52wrx" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://osf.io/jum2f/files/52wrx</a></span></span></span> In our release, we point to their file names and do not release their images. We release our data alongside our code on github,<span id="footnote3" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">3</span>
              
              
              
              
              
              
              
            <a href="https://github.com/sally-xu-42/cross-modal-taxonomic-gen" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/sally-xu-42/cross-modal-taxonomic-gen</a></span></span></span> which uses an MIT License.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Data Statistics</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A2.F8" title="In B.2 Data Statistics ‣ Appendix B Details of Experimental Data ‣ Cross-Modal Taxonomic Generalization in (Vision-) Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> shows the distribution of the number of hypernyms per leaf, and <a href="#A2.F9" title="In B.2 Data Statistics ‣ Appendix B Details of Experimental Data ‣ Cross-Modal Taxonomic Generalization in (Vision-) Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> shows the number of leaves across all 53 hypernyms in the dataset.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A2.T2" title="In B.2 Data Statistics ‣ Appendix B Details of Experimental Data ‣ Cross-Modal Taxonomic Generalization in (Vision-) Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> reports the dataset statistics under five levels of random hypernym ablation and three data variants.
For each ablation level, we show the number of image-question pairs in the training, validation, and test sets, with validation and test sets further divided into leaf-level, seen-hypernym, and unseen-hypernym subsets.
The <span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">original</span> variant corresponds to the unshuffled dataset.
The <span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">across-category</span> and <span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">within-category</span> variants are obtained by shuffling hypernym annotations across categories or within the same category, with details listed in <a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3 On the Arbitrariness of Cross-Modal Taxonomic Generalization ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Cross-Modal Taxonomic Generalization in (Vision-) Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a> and <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Shuffling Algorithms ‣ Cross-Modal Taxonomic Generalization in (Vision-) Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>.
Across all ablation levels and data variants, the images in the test set are held fixed.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F8" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2603.07474v1/hypernym-counts.svg" id="A2.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:381/309;" width="381" height="309"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 8: </span>Distribution of the number of hypernym categories per leaf in our dataset. Counts (y-axis) are log-scaled.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A2.F9" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2603.07474v1/hypernym-distribution.svg" id="A2.F9.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/174;" width="476" height="174"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 9: </span>Number of leaves per hypernym category. Counts (y-axis) are log-scaled.</figcaption>
</figure>
