<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>Data statistics under <math id="A2.T2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> random hypernym ablation levels and counterfactual data variants. “I-Q pair” refers to an image and associated yes-no question. “Seen” and “Unseen” indicate the number of seen and unseen hypernym I-Q pairs, respectively. “# Leaves affected” is the number of leaf categories that have had any I-Q pairs removed,
accounting for duplicates (removal under multiple hypernyms), and rounding.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A2.T3" title="In B.2 Data Statistics ‣ Appendix B Details of Experimental Data ‣ Cross-Modal Taxonomic Generalization in (Vision-) Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> reports dataset statistics under systematic hypernym ablation at four ablation levels.
In contrast to random ablation, systematic hypernym ablation removes entire hypernym categories from the training data.</p>
</div>
